//   (A reflection's glint reads the eye's direction as it must: the low sun on the river and on glaze.)
// WHAT READS THE PIXEL'S FOOTPRINT, AND ONLY AS A FILTER (section 153; none of it builds, moves, hides or shrinks a
//   thing): the brick's, the paving's, the bark's, the glaze's and the planted floor's patterns go into their means
