// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the planting (a plan by rows and plots; INVENTED as the brief says)
// THE PLAN. Every tree stands on a PIER'S LINE (x = pierX(j)): under it the pier is hollow and filled with earth, as
// Strabo has it, so a tree's earth is as deep as the pier is high; between the piers' lines the earth over a vault's
// crown is 1.0 m (1.8 m on the first terrace) and carries herbs and vines only. The feeder channels run north over
