// (r8, ROOM MADE: the swallows' flights are six, five and five birds where r7 had nine, seven and six.)
// BIRDS: every flock flies one closed loop on the world clock. Every loop is laid from the places it joins (a nest,
// a reed bar, the moat, a wall's top, a row of trunks), by their own constants, off the flown line by its flock's own
// reach and more (flockReach: the count reads the loop and what is handed to the kit, nothing else; the kit shrinks a
// bird that comes within 5.39 m (storks with their own coats), 2.76 m (egrets with their own coats) or 1.6 m
// (others) of the eye, by the kit's own law, and no bird's place comes so
// near the line). A kind that should be about at every
// clock flies as several flights at even shares of one loop (set: its flights' number); the whole set's place on
// the loop is one seeded draw (flockStarts), and a flock with no set is started by the kit's own seeded draw.
// The flown line's share is handed to no flock: a closed loop goes by the clock alone.
const DOVE_COAT = { body: '#b8b4b0', belly: '#d8d4cc', wingC: '#9a969a', tip: '#5a5860', tailC: '#8a868c', head: '#a8a4a8' };
// a stork: white, its flight feathers black, bill and legs red, neck out and legs trailing; an egret: smaller, all
// white, a yellow bill, dark legs (each its own measures on the kit's long-necked flier; no pink on either)
const STORK = { len: 0.8, girth: 0.12, span: 0.95, chord: 0.3, neck: 0.42, legs: 0.62, body: '#f2efe8', belly: '#fbf9f4', wingC: '#f0ece4', trail: '#1c1a1c', tip: '#1c1a1c', tailC: '#f2efe8', beak: '#c8442c', head: '#f2efe8', neckC: '#f2efe8', legC: '#d05a3a' };
const EGRET = { len: 0.5, girth: 0.08, span: 0.62, chord: 0.22, neck: 0.3, legs: 0.5, body: '#f6f4ee', belly: '#fdfcf8', wingC: '#f4f2ec', trail: '#f0eee8', tip: '#f0eee8', tailC: '#f6f4ee', beak: '#d8a83c', head: '#f6f4ee', neckC: '#f6f4ee', legC: '#2a2a28' };
// a flying egret is the bird that stands in the shallows: the kit's wading egret has a body of 0.4 m and a neck of
// 0.42 m; the flier's measures above times EGRET_SIZE give a body of 0.56 m with the neck drawn in, a wing of 0.7 m
// (at the kit's own size of 0.75 the flier would be two thirds of the standing bird). The flights' spacing is given in
// metres, so the size does not change it
const EGRET_SIZE = 1.12;
const MOAT_Z = (f) => lerp(BANK_S, -(M.CANAL_W + M.WALL_T), f), WALL_MID_Z = -(M.CANAL_W + M.WALL_T / 2), T_Y = (n, up) => M.TER_Y[n] + up;
const ROW_N = M.WALK_Z - M.ROW_OFF - 1, ROW_S = M.WALK_Z + M.ROW_OFF + 1, GAP_MID = (GAP_X0 + GAP_X1) / 2, BAR_Z = (MOUTH_BAR.Z0 + MOUTH_BAR.Z1) / 2;
// WHICH FLOCKS ARE ALSO HANDED keepClear, AND WITH WHAT (the crew's kit text; the owner's kit text on its cost). IN
// THIS TREE IT IS HANDED TO NOTHING: this tree's kit (the older engine) reads no keepClear, so here these flocks
// fly their loops as the others do and nothing is steered clear of the way; the owner's engine reads it (the
// designer's word; we have not run it). A flock whose air comes within FLOCK_KEEP.NEAR metres of the visitor's way
// carries keep: the stretch of that way, in metres from its start, that the flock's air comes near. The kit is
// handed the way's own points of that stretch alone (it has nothing to keep clear of where the birds never are). A
// STRETCH IS TWO OF THE FLIGHT'S OWN MARKS (makeFlight: each the metre where the lens comes abreast of a standing
// thing); no metre of the route is typed here:
//   the stair's foot: the moat's swallows turn over the landing, abreast of the stair's first steps (a loop of the
//     clock): from the quay's edge, where the way comes in over the landing platform, to the first flight's head
//   the walk: the trunk swallows go down the two rows from the court to the door: from the mark bandE (the line
//     is east of the planted band's east wall: with r8's line that is where it comes over the top terrace's lip
//     into the court) to the line's own end before the door
//   the gap: the wing's doves pass the open south row: from the court's east edge to the gap's east jamb (the gap's
//     west jamb lies 3.75 m east of the court's edge: the stretch begins at the nearest mark west of that jamb)
